# PM2 ecosystem config is TRACKED, deliberately. It was excluded as
# "server-specific", but it holds no secrets — public NEXT_PUBLIC_* values
# and a loopback backend URL — and being untracked meant the cluster
# settings that keep deploys from dropping requests existed in exactly one
# place, on one droplet, recoverable from nothing.
#   ecosystem.config.js

# Kept on the server beside the code, never in the repo. Untracked files here
# used to block `git pull` the moment a commit landed on the same path — which
# broke two deploys on 2026-08-31 — so they are ignored explicitly rather than
# left to chance.
# One-off scripts run once against production, kept for reference.
backend/scratch/
# Local vector store.
backend/chromadb_data/
*.bak
.env*.bak*

# Playwright output. frontend/.gitignore already covers frontend/test-results,
# but its rules are anchored with a leading slash and so do not reach a run that
# lands at the repo root — which is where an interrupted mobile-suite run puts
# .last-run.json. Ignored here too so a stray run cannot leave the tree dirty.
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/playwright/.cache/
